From d16128c8619a9d48a83c9cdf0c55980baca6d18b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:31:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: optical: add GN28L9x support

Extend the existing Semtech provider to share lower-page SFF diagnostics,
alarm decoding, frontend registration and hwmon across the GN25 and GN28
families without changing the existing module or Kconfig symbol names.

Add a GN28L96-specific initialization path based on Final Data Sheet
Rev.9. Verify the chip identity, preserve factory EEPROM calibration,
and load board-specific MCU calibration into tables 80 through 86.
Validate firmware before writing, hold software TX_DISABLE during
calibration, verify readback before committing the startup key, and
leave transmitter enable to the protocol consumer. Normalize hardware
TX_DISABLE, TX_FAULT and LOS/SD polarity in frontend state reporting.

GN28L98 remains an experimental, read-only preconfigured SFF frontend.
Do not infer its vendor registers or calibration from another model.
Document the firmware format, device-tree setup and remaining limits.

Validation: W=1 object builds for ARMv7 LE, MIPS32r2 BE/LE and x86;
DT schema and example checks; 733 injected I2C failures, calibration
readback corruption, invalid firmware and readiness timeout checks;
2048 status/polarity combinations using mocked register access.
No optical hardware or OLT validation was performed.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
